Implement and compare at least two candidates: one that changes the hinge swing while preserving its location, and another that tests a different hinge or doorway placement with a coherent leaf assembly. First use a diagnostic view or visibility render to distinguish wall hiding from an edge-on camera projection. Compare each candidate's rendered leaf outline, exposed face and overlap with the floor and doorway against the reference, keeping the camera fixed for the initial comparison. Inspect top and side views for wall or furniture intersections and lost hinge alignment. If neither candidate works, test camera-relative framing separately and check whether the bed and shelving landmarks deteriorate.
